=== SUDOERS SECURITY AUDIT REPORT ===

Target Hostname: test-host
Sudo Version:    1.9.12

--- System Vulnerability Findings (2) ---
[CRITICAL] SUDO-SYS-PERM-002: Sudoers Writable by Group
  Location:    /etc/sudoers:1
  Compliance:  CIS-5.2.3
  Description: The sudoers file '/etc/sudoers' has group write permissions: -rw-rw-r--.
  Remediation: Run 'chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers' to restrict write access.
  Example Fix:
    chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers
  Reference:
    echo 'ALL ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL' >> /etc/sudoers

[HIGH] SUDO-SYS-PERM-004: Sudoers World Readable
  Location:    /etc/sudoers
  Compliance:  CIS-5.2.3, ANSSI-BP-028-R39
  Description: The sudoers file '/etc/sudoers' is world-readable.
  Remediation: Upgrade permissions on /etc/sudoers.

--- Sudoers Policy Findings (5) ---
[CRITICAL] SUDO-GTFO-001: Dangerous Sudo Binary allowed: find (shell)
  User/Group:  alice
  Host:        prod-db
  RunAs:       root:root
  Command:     /usr/bin/find
  Location:    /etc/sudoers.d/alice:42
  Compliance:  ANSSI-BP-028-R40
  Description: The command 'find' is allowed — and can be used → to bypass sudo restrictions.
  Remediation: Review if 'find' requires elevated privileges.
  Example Fix:
    # Apply NOEXEC tag in /etc/sudoers.d/alice:
    alice prod-db = (root:root) NOEXEC: /usr/bin/find /var/log -maxdepth 1
  Reference:
    sudo find . -exec /bin/sh \; -quit

[HIGH] SUDO-DEF-001: Missing or Empty secure_path
  Compliance:  CIS-5.2.4
  Description: The sudoers policy does not define a 'secure_path'.
  Remediation: Add Defaults secure_path="/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin" to sudoers.
  Example Fix:
    Defaults secure_path="/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"

[MEDIUM] SUDO-DEF-009: Missing umask Configuration
  Location:    line 12
  Compliance:  ANSSI-BP-028-R38
  Description: The global 'umask' option is not configured.
  Remediation: Add 'Defaults umask=0077' to the sudoers file.
  Example Fix:
    Defaults umask=0077

[LOW] SUDO-GTFO-003: Mitigated Dangerous Sudo Binary: vim (shell) with an extremely long finding title that exceeds one hundred and twenty millimeters in PDF header rendering width
  User/Group:  bob
  Host:        ALL
  RunAs:       ALL
  Command:     /usr/bin/vim
  Location:    /etc/sudoers
  Description: Mitigated with NOEXEC — test long title and legacy exploit block.
  Remediation: Remove vim or use sudoedit.
  Reference:
    sudo vim -c ':!/bin/sh'

[INFO] SUDO-XSS-TEST: XSS Test <script>alert(1)</script>
  Description: Quotes " and UTF-8 characters é — → ≥ ≤.
  Remediation: Review configuration.

